Tested Instanton geometries and Hessian matrices
----------------------------------------------------------------------
For the instanton geometries and Hessian matrix, we rely on the
numpy-accessible outputs. 

These have been tested against Yair Litman's in-the-house independent implementation (2020).

Implicit bath has been tested against explicit bath calculations (Dec 2023)

BUGFIX: 100K_implicit_friction frequency conversion and proton mass
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The y/z spring constant uses the incorrect conversion divisor 219323.
Use i-PI's standard conversion divisor of approximately 219474.6291 instead.
Also replace the hardcoded masses used in these y/z spring constants
(1836 and 1837.36223469) with the CODATA 2022 proton mass, 1836.152673426
in atomic units (proton-electron mass ratio).
Source: https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?mpsme
The saved Hessian contains the old spring constant even though y and z
coordinates are zero. Validate and regenerate the Hessian reference when
correcting these constants.
